<article class="ws-sheet">
<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 9th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 800s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/9th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 850 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10683 5623" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 850 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="6134" cy="1224" r="182"/><text x="6134" y="1301" font-size="218">1</text></g><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="182"/><text x="5709" y="1046" font-size="218">2</text></g><g><circle cx="7771" cy="1192" r="182"/><text x="7771" y="1269" font-size="218">3</text></g><g><circle cx="7097" cy="1795" r="182"/><text x="7097" y="1871" font-size="218">4</text></g><g><circle cx="4881" cy="1071" r="182"/><text x="4881" y="1148" font-size="218">5</text></g><g><circle cx="7833" cy="2434" r="182"/><text x="7833" y="2510" font-size="218">6</text></g><g><circle cx="4782" cy="1851" r="182"/><text x="4782" y="1927" font-size="218">7</text></g><g><circle cx="5229" cy="694" r="182"/><text x="5229" y="771" font-size="218">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 850 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Byzantine Empire &middot; Holy Roman Empire &middot; Rashtrakuta dynasty &middot; Ghana Empire &middot; Srivijaya Empire &middot; Tang Dynasty &middot; Abbasid Caliphate &middot; Emirate of Córdoba</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Edington</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Ostia</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Coronation of Charlemagne</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Ellendun</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Anarchy at Samarra</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Treaty of Verdun</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Charles the Bald</li><li>Alfred the Great</li><li>Árpád</li><li>Ansgar</li><li>Rhodri the Great</li><li>Boso of Provence</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 845–c. 907</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>801–865</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 844–887</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>823–877</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>849–899</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 820–878</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Chao (currency)</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Mounted archer</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 800s, 175 recorded states were founded and 96 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Abbasid Caliphate, the Byzantine Empire and the Tang Dynasty. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 9th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/9th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 9th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Abbasid Caliphate <span>750 CE – 1517 CE</span></li><li>Byzantine Empire <span>330 CE – 1453 CE</span></li><li>Tang Dynasty <span>618 CE – 907 CE</span></li><li>Rashtrakuta dynasty <span>753 CE – 982 CE</span></li><li>Emirate of Córdoba <span>756 CE – 929 CE</span></li><li>Srivijaya Empire <span>650 CE – 1377 CE</span></li><li>Ghana Empire <span>300 CE – 1240 CE</span></li><li>Holy Roman Empire <span>800 CE – 1806 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Coronation of Charlemagne <span>800 CE</span></li><li>Battle of Ellendun <span>825</span></li><li>Treaty of Verdun <span>843 CE</span></li><li>Battle of Ostia <span>849</span></li><li>Anarchy at Samarra <span>861–870</span></li><li>Battle of Edington <span>878</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Charles the Bald <span>4: 823–877</span></li><li>Alfred the Great <span>5: 849–899</span></li><li>Árpád <span>1: c. 845–c. 907</span></li><li>Ansgar <span>2: 801–865</span></li><li>Rhodri the Great <span>6: c. 820–878</span></li><li>Boso of Provence <span>3: c. 844–887</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Chao (currency)</dt><dd>Chao was the paper currency issued by the Yuan Dynasty in China.</dd><dt>Mounted archer</dt><dd>A mounted archer is a cavalry soldier who shoots arrows from horseback.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
